      "sample_index": 2,
      "text": "To find the length of segment \\( BC \\) in triangle \\( ABC \\), we will first use the given information and the Pythagorean theorem.\n\nGiven:\n- Triangle \\( ABC \\) is a right triangle with \\( AB \\) adjacent to the right angle and hypotenuse \\( AC \\).\n- Triangle \\( ABD \\) is also a right triangle with \\( AD \\) adjacent to the right angle and hypotenuse \\( AD \\).\n\nFirst, we find the length of \\( AB \\). Since \\( AB \\) is adjacent to the right angle in both triangles and we know \\( AB = 19 \\), we can use the Pythagorean theorem in triangle \\( ABC \\).\n\nLet \\( BC = x \\) and \\( AC = 37 \\). According to the Pythagorean theorem:\n\\[\nAB^2 + BC^2 = AC^2\n\\]\nSubstituting the known values:\n\\[\n19^2 + x^2 = 37^2\n\\]\n\\[\n361 + x^2 = 1369\n\\]\nSubtract 361 from both sides:\n\\[\nx^2 = 1008\n\\]\nTaking the square root of both sides:\n\\[\nx = \\sqrt{1008} = \\sqrt{144 \\times 7} = 12\\sqrt{7}\n\\]\n\nThus, the length of segment \\( BC \\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{12\\sqrt{7}}\n\\]",
